es-rgds-memory: glibc's allocator keeps less, and gives the menu's freed memory back before a game

The menu once grew to 713 MB on an RG DS Plus (975 MB RAM, no swap) and was OOM-killed after the handheld had been
unreachable for minutes (2026-10-05; not reproduced in ten game round trips since). Whatever grew, glibc made it stick:
images are decoded at full size on several threads, freed buffers stay in per-thread arenas (up to eight per core),
and after its first big free glibc raises its mmap threshold, so later big buffers come from those arenas as well.
ES now runs with two arenas and maps every buffer from 256 KB up on its own, which goes back to the system when freed
(MALLOC_ARENA_MAX / MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_ in the environment still decide when set), and trims the heap
(malloc_trim) right before a game starts, so the game gets what the menu freed. The rnds engine's texture cache has
a byte budget of its own (es-rgds-rnds.patch).

diff --git a/es-app/src/main.cpp b/es-app/src/main.cpp
index 75714e3d..056a703f 100644
--- a/es-app/src/main.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/main.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@
 #include "Paths.h"
 #include "resources/TextureData.h"
 #include "resources/TextureResource.h"
+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
+#include <malloc.h>
+#endif
 #include "Scripting.h"
 #include "watchers/WatchersManager.h"
 #include "HttpReq.h"
@@ -488,6 +491,17 @@ int main(int argc, char* argv[])
 {
 	// Utils::MathExpr::performUnitTests();
 
+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
+	// ROCKNIXDS (es-rgds-memory): the menu once grew to 713 MB on an RG DS Plus (975 MB, no swap) and was OOM-killed
+	// after minutes of thrashing. Images are decoded at full size on several threads, and glibc then keeps freed
+	// buffers in per-thread arenas (up to 8 per core) and, past its first big free, raises its mmap threshold so later
+	// big buffers come from those arenas too: the process only grows. Two arenas, and buffers from 256 KB up mapped
+	// on their own (returned to the system when freed). MALLOC_ARENA_MAX / MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_ in the environment
+	// still win (glibc reads them first; mallopt here only fills in the unset ones).
+	if (!getenv("MALLOC_ARENA_MAX")) mallopt(M_ARENA_MAX, 2);
+	if (!getenv("MALLOC_MMAP_THRESHOLD_")) mallopt(M_MMAP_THRESHOLD, 256 * 1024);
+#endif
+
 #ifdef WIN32
 	// Must run before any window/message-queue APIs are touched.
 	Utils::Platform::setDpiAwareness();
diff --git a/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp b/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp
index af899d99..ff8abda1 100644
--- a/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,9 @@
 #include "guis/GuiMsgBox.h"
 #include "utils/ThreadPool.h"
 #include <SDL_timer.h>
+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
+#include <malloc.h>
+#endif
 #include "TextToSpeech.h"
 #include "VolumeControl.h"
 #include "guis/GuiNetPlay.h"
@@ -479,6 +482,9 @@ bool ViewController::doLaunchGame(FileData* game, LaunchGameOptions options)
 	// Silence TTS when launching a game
 	TextToSpeech::getInstance()->say(" ");
 
+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
+	malloc_trim(0);	// ROCKNIXDS (es-rgds-memory): what the menu freed goes back to the system before the game needs it
+#endif
 	bool reload = game->launchGame(mWindow, options) && game->getSourceFileData()->getSystemName() == "windows_installers";
 	sLastGameEndedAt = monoMs();
 	return reload;
